# 7. DATABASE SOURCE-OF-TRUTH ARCHITECTURE

This is a critical requirement.

## Google Sheets remains the authoritative business database.

The system must respect Kawad Swad's established database architecture and source-of-truth requirements.

Google Sheets is the authoritative source of business records.

MongoDB, local caches, browser storage, temporary state, or secondary databases must NOT silently become the sole authoritative source of business data.

Secondary storage may be used where appropriate for:

- Cache
- Temporary processing
- Sessions
- Queueing
- Operational metadata
- Performance
- Non-authoritative technical data

But the architecture must preserve the defined source-of-truth model.

## Existing Google Apps Script Gateway

A separate Google Apps Script gateway already exists and is part of the wider system architecture.

Do not blindly create a new gateway or replace the existing integration.

Investigate the existing integration from the source, available configuration, documentation, and relevant code.

Build the ERP around the established gateway architecture where appropriate.

If some gateway code is not available in the ZIP:

- Identify the missing component.
- Determine its expected interface.
- Make the ERP integration compatible with it.
- Create the necessary integration contracts.
- Do not invent claims that the gateway has been tested when it has not.

